WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.460
Most of Game of Thrones happens in Westeros
– home to the Starks and Lannisters, the

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.640
Wall and the Iron Throne. But Daenerys’
story starts in the eastern continent of Essos

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.700
– with the Dothraki Sea, and Slaver’s
Bay. We also see Braavos, Pentos, Volantis,

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.010
Valyria in the show, and Qarth. But the world
of Game of Thrones is far bigger than we see

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:27.310
in the series. The worldbook describes far
distant cities and kingdoms, with their own

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:32.680
cultures, histories, and mysteries. Some of
the strangest places are in the far east of

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:39.870
Essos, and in the southern continent of Sothoryos.
Sothoryos is full of jungle, ruined cities,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.699
and mystery. No one knows how big it is. A
dragonrider once spent three years flying

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:49.880
over the continent, but she never found its
southern border – said it’s “a land

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.300
without end” . Colonies on Sothoryos have
all failed , and treasure-hunters don’t

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:01.619
return . Cause the jungles are full of disease
– blood boils, sweetrot, wormbone, Red Death

00:01:01.619 --> 00:01:07.640
. Archmaester Ebrose says that disease kills
half of all Westerosi visitors . And those

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.920
who survive the sickness are often killed
by the wildlife. There are “Huge crocodiles”,

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:18.590
“carnivorous fish”, snakes, and basilisks,
and apes so huge they can kill elephants with

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:24.800
one punch . The only animal that isn’t deadly
is the purple-eyed lemur, called the Little

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.490
Valyrian . Further south, in the Green Hell
regions, are said to be vampire bats that

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:36.260
can drain a man of blood, and tattooed lizards
with claws on their legs , like some kinda

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:41.320
dinosaurs. “Most terrible of all are the
wyverns”, which are similar to dragons.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:46.980
They don’t breathe fire, but they’re angrier
to make up for it . Some kinds hunt in packs

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.960
of a hundred , or use stealthy black scales
to sneak crit their prey . And if somehow

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.540
you survive the wildlife and the disease,
there are slavers prowling the coast . And

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:03.570
there are the native Sothoryi, called Brindled
Men. They’re hairy, big-boned, “massively

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:08.789
muscled” “creatures”, with noses like
snouts, and thick skin like a hog, coloured

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:14.799
white and brown – Brindled Men can’t reproduce
with other humans . The Brindled Men near

00:02:14.799 --> 00:02:19.390
the coast have learned to speak the local
“trade talk”. But the Men further south

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:24.590
are said to be “savage” cannibals, who
worship dark gods . It’s said there were

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:31.090
once lizard men, and eyeless cave-dwellers
– old races who were destroyed or devoured

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:38.049
by the Brindled Men . But the greatest mystery
of Sothoryos is Yeen. Yeen is a ruined city,

00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:44.069
“older than time” and built from massive
blocks of “oily black stone”. No trees

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:50.150
or vines touch it – it’s “A city so
evil that even the jungle will not enter”

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:56.280
. When Princess Nymeria tried to settle some
Rhoynar in Yeen, the entire population “vanished

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.140
overnight” .
So that’s Sothoryos. Off its western coast

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:06.299
are the Basilisk Isles – “the festering
sore of the Summer Sea”. Hot and humid,

00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:12.379
the Isles swarm “with stinging flies, sand
fleas, and bloodworms” . Old Valyria used

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:18.329
an isle as a penal colony for their “worst
criminals”. In their city of Gogossos, Valyrian

00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:23.909
“torturers devised new torments”, and
practiced “blood sorcery”, mating “beasts”

00:03:23.909 --> 00:03:31.010
“to slave women” to birth “twisted half-human
children” . It’s actually crazy how often

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.650
“half-human children” are mentioned in
the books . It’s possible that ancient inter-species

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:41.870
breeding is what gives Targaryens their dragon
magic, and the Starks their warging powers.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:46.980
It’s also possible that some of these twisted
monsters on Sothoryos might have been created

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:53.640
by Valyrian blood magic. There’s some weird
shit in the books. Anyway, after the Doom,

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.970
Gogossos grew “rich and powerful” on slavery
and sorcery , until it was wiped out in a

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:04.450
plague . Eventually, people returned – and
the Isles are now home to pirates, in towns

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:10.200
with names like “Sty”, “Whore’s Gash”
and “Black Pudding” . They have charming

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:15.280
local customs, like piling the skulls of their
enemies on an island “as an offering to

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.229
some dark god” . Occasionally, the Free
Cities come to wipe out the pirates, but the

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:25.700
pirates always come back. One time, a captain
called Saathos Saan was sent to destroy the

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:32.569
pirates, and instead he became a pirate king
who ruled for thirty years . Saathos Saan

00:04:32.569 --> 00:04:38.910
is an ancestor of Davos’ friend Salladhor
Saan. Also, in Book 5, Barristan Selmy trains

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:43.840
a boy from the Basilisk Isles, called Tumco
Lho – and Barristan says he’s “the best

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:49.080
natural swordsman” he’d seen “since
Jaime Lannister” , which is high praise.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:55.060
One of the Basilisk Isles features an “ancient
idol” of a “gigantic toad” of “malignant

00:04:55.060 --> 00:05:00.980
aspect”. The statue is forty feet high,
and carved of “greasy black stone”. The

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:06.490
people of Toad Isle have “an unpleasant
fishlike aspect to their faces, and many have

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:12.780
webbed hands and feet” . So like Yeen, this
is a reference to H. P. Lovecraft, who wrote

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:19.169
about strange fishy people worshipping strange
fishy gods. These “black stone” structures

00:05:19.169 --> 00:05:24.039
are scattered all over the world of Thrones,
and it’s hinted that they were built by

00:05:24.039 --> 00:05:29.190
a Lovecraftian fish people called the “Deep
Ones” – whose descendants apparently still

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:37.289
live on the Toad Isle. So in conclusion, the
worldbook says, the Basilisk Isles are “best

00:05:37.289 --> 00:05:40.080
avoided” .
Thousands of years ago, in the grasslands

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:46.320
of Essos, the first civilisations began . Legend
says that a Silver Sea was ruled by Fisher

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:52.279
Queens from a floating palace . There were
savage Hairy Men who rode to battle on unicorns

00:05:52.279 --> 00:05:57.409
, and a city of Lyber where “acolytes of
a spider goddess” warred against those of

00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:02.370
“a serpent god” . It’s said there was
a kingdom of centaurs – who might have actually

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:07.659
been “mounted warriors” . These are just
ancient legends, but we do know there was

00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:14.039
a kingdom called Sarnor. The Sarnori called
themselves Tall Men, and they were “Warriors,

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:19.569
sorcerers, and scholars” . They built cities
across the grasslands, with canals, caravans

00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:25.629
and libraries, worshipping a “hundred gods”
. Sarnori soldiers “wore steel and spider

00:06:25.629 --> 00:06:31.229
silk”, and rode “scythed chariots” , with
women and men fighting together . Sarnor warred

00:06:31.229 --> 00:06:37.050
against the Qaathi, and the Dothraki, and
even fought in Valyria’s wars against Ghis

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:41.400
. The Sarnori were divided into lots of rival
kingdoms, but traditionally they were ruled

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:47.199
by a High King in a wondrous Palace With a
Thousand Rooms . Legend says that the first

00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:53.039
High King was called Huzhor Amai, which sounds
like Azor Ahai, the hero who ended the Long

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:58.250
Night . Many of the cultures of Essos have
their own versions of that story – it’s

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.879
like how Noah’s ark and the Epic of Gilgamesh
tell different versions of the same flood

00:07:02.879 --> 00:07:08.750
myth . Sarnor dominated the west grasslands
for thousands of years . But after the Doom

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:15.420
of Valyria, the Dothraki united, and attacked
Sarnor in force. City after city fell, and

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:20.620
Sarnor was too slow and divided to fight the
threat . They were broken in a final battle

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:26.840
called the Field of Crows. Now, their kingdom
lies in ruins, and fewer than twenty thousand

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.759
Tall Men remain .
North of Essos is a vast ocean called the

00:07:31.759 --> 00:07:38.009
Shivering Sea. It’s full of fish, crabs,
seals , whales, and leviathans the size of

00:07:38.009 --> 00:07:43.550
islands . Sailors also describe mermaids,
and “drowned spirits”, and mists that

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:50.009
can instantly freeze a whole ship. There are
many reports of ice dragons, “colossal beasts”

00:07:50.009 --> 00:07:55.080
much bigger than regular dragons. They’re
made of living ice , and breathe cold instead

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:01.050
of flame – which might explain the freezing
mists. When ice dragons die, they melt, so

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:07.139
no one can prove they exist . In the far north
is an arctic waste where the blizzards never

00:08:07.139 --> 00:08:12.830
end. Sailors describe strange lights in the
sky, which might be aurora borealis. They

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:18.539
are also tales of Cannibal Bay, where ships
enter, then are trapped when the sea freezes

00:08:18.539 --> 00:08:24.229
behind them . It’s said that “a thousand
ships lie entombed in Cannibal Bay”, “still

00:08:24.229 --> 00:08:29.199
inhabited by the children and grandchildren
of their original crews”, “who survive

00:08:29.199 --> 00:08:35.650
by feasting [on] the flesh of sailors newly
caught” . Much of the Shivering Sea is ruled

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:41.310
by the people of the island of Ib .
The Ibbenese are short, strong , and hairy

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:46.990
, with ridged brows and massive jaws . Ibbenese
can sometimes reproduce with other humans,

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:52.560
but the offspring are sterile . So like the
Brindled Men, the Ibbenese might be another

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:58.320
species of human – kinda like how Neanderthals
lived alongside homo sapiens in the real world

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:04.130
for a while. The Ibbenese are cunning craftsmen,
hunters and warriors who fish the Shivering

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:09.480
Sea. Their whaling ships are renowned for
their strength in weathering storms, and taking

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:16.000
whales for bone, blubber and oil. The island
of Ib has of dark forests and mountains, full

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.839
of bears, wolves, and mammoths. Many Ibbenese
live alone in these woods as foresters or

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:28.060
miners. But others live in the main Port of
Ibben, in the shadow of the God-King’s castle,

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:34.430
a “colossal” ruin that once housed “a
hundred Ibbenese kings” . Under the God-Kings,

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:39.990
Ib conquered the forests to the south, which
were inhabited by “a small, shy forest folk”

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:45.300
called the Ifequevron, or woods walkers. The
woods walkers are thought to be related to

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:50.050
the children of the forest of Westeros – the
woods walkers “carved trees”, like how

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:55.250
the children carve weirwoods. But the woods
walkers also built a “settlement” or “City”

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.940
, which is cool, cause we’ve never seen
a city built by the children in Westeros.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:05.090
The God-Kings are gone now, and Ib’s ruled
by a council of nobles. But the woods walkers

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:10.550
are said to still live in the deeper woods,
and will bless a household that leaves offerings

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:15.040
of leaf and stone.
East of Ib, we start getting into the really

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.839
distant lands. Author George Martin warns
us that we’re seeing this world from the

00:10:19.839 --> 00:10:27.329
perspective of Westerosi maesters, whose information
on distant places might be inaccurate. Distortions

00:10:27.329 --> 00:10:33.100
and errors creep in – ‘here be dragons’
type stuff. So everything from here on in

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:39.810
might be mixed with myth. East of Ib are said
to be the Thousand Islands, a scatter of bleak

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:45.380
windswept rocks. They’re inhabited by a
strange hairless people with green skin and

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:51.670
teeth filed to sharp points. They’re said
to sacrifice sailors to fish-headed gods , but

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:57.370
they’re so afraid of the sea that they won’t
touch the water, “even under threat of death”.

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:02.410
Some say the Thousand Islands are “the last
remnants of a drowned kingdom whose towns

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:08.110
and towers were submerged” thousands of
years ago . So again, this stuff is straight

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:14.750
outta Lovecraft. South of the Thousand Islands
is the port city of Nefer, surrounded by cliffs,

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:21.100
and shrouded in fog. Nefer looks like a small
town, but most of the city is hidden underground

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:27.440
– so Nefer is called “the Secret City”,
known for necromancy and torture . East of

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:33.139
Nefer are the “grim, grey” forests of
Mossovy , a “dark land of shapechangers

00:11:33.139 --> 00:11:39.269
and demon hunters” . These mysterious lands
are as far east as any Westerosi has been

00:11:39.269 --> 00:11:42.880
.
Essos is divided by a great mountain range

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:48.279
called the Bones, named for the remains of
those who try to cross them . The mountains

00:11:48.279 --> 00:11:55.009
are riddled with rivers, canyons, vast underground
caverns and sunless seas . There are passes

00:11:55.009 --> 00:11:59.230
into the mountains – “ancient carved steps”
and “hidden … passages” . But only a

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:04.699
few roads lead out of the Bones – the Steel
Road, the Stone Road and the Sand Road . Each

00:12:04.699 --> 00:12:11.899
of these are guarded by a fortress city – Kayakayanaya,
Samyriana and Bayasabhad. These cities were

00:12:11.899 --> 00:12:16.470
once outposts of the “kingdom of Hyrkoon”.
But the lakes and rivers of Hyrkoon dried

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:23.329
up, reducing the kingdom to ruin . Now, only
these three cities remain, defended by warrior

00:12:23.329 --> 00:12:28.230
women who believe that only “those who give
birth” are “permitted to take life”

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:32.839
. The woman “wear iron rings in their nipples
and rubies in their cheeks”, and are trained

00:12:32.839 --> 00:12:39.330
in combat from childhood. Most men in these
cities are gelded, and live as eunuchs – only

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:44.410
the strongest and handsomest men are allowed
to breed, and to rule the cities , making

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:49.970
the Bones a confusing mix of matriarchy and
patriarchy.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:55.329
East of the Bones are the plains of the Jogos
Nhai. These guys are a bit like Dothraki – nomadic

00:12:55.329 --> 00:13:01.339
mounted warriors roaming across grasslands
. But the Jogos Nhai don’t ride horses – they

00:13:01.339 --> 00:13:07.190
ride zorses, which in the real world are hybrids
of zebras and horses . The zorses of Game

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:12.680
of Thrones are similar, but tend to be tough
and angry . There’s a book character called

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:18.480
Vargo Hoat who rides a zorse in Westeros – he
leads the Brave Companions who cut off Jaime

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:24.509
Lannister’s hand in Book 3. But the Jogos
Nhai are short and squat, with pointed skulls

00:13:24.509 --> 00:13:29.649
because they bind their heads when young – which
is actually a thing in the real world . Groups

00:13:29.649 --> 00:13:34.720
of Jogos Nhai are ruled by a war chief and
a moonsinger. Usually the chiefs are men,

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:39.240
and the moonsingers women, but sometimes they
switch roles, and live as the other gender

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:44.959
. Because of their religion, the Jogos Nhai
don’t kill other Jogos Nhai. But they constantly

00:13:44.959 --> 00:13:50.300
wage war on the peoples around them – including
the cities of the Bones. It’s said that

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:55.380
the Jogos Nhai wiped out the last of the “stone
giants” , who were “twice as large as

00:13:55.380 --> 00:14:02.440
the giants of Westeros” , which’d make’m
like 24 feet or seven metres tall. The Jogos

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:08.140
also fight Yi Ti – an empire to the south
. Sick of being raided, the YiTish have tried

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:14.100
to wipe out the Jogos Nhai, and one time they
got close, under Emperor Lo Bu. But a Jogos

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:19.690
warrior woman called Zhea rose up and destroyed
Lo Bu’s armies, claiming the Emperor’s

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:24.650
skull as “her drinking cup” .
Yi Ti is “the oldest and greatest of the

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:31.180
eastern civilizations” – inspired by imperial
China . A land of hills and plains, jungles

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:36.550
and rainforests , it’s said to be so wealthy
that its princes live in houses of solid gold

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:43.079
. Its forests are dense, and said to be infested
with basilisks , but a web of stone roads

00:14:43.079 --> 00:14:49.160
provides safe passage . The cities of Yi Ti
more magnificent than anywhere in Westeros

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:54.830
– the current emperor lives in a palace
that’s larger than the entire city of King’s

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.920
Landing . So Yi Ti is crazy powerful, and
legend says that thousands of years ago, it

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:06.079
was even greater. The “Great Empire of the
Dawn” covered most of far east Essos, with

00:15:06.079 --> 00:15:12.010
riches and armies even greater than the Valyrian
empire . The first emperor of Yi Ti was believed

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:17.980
to be a god on earth – son of the Lion of
Night and the Maiden-Made-of-Light. It’s

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:23.750
said that this first god-emperor ruled for
ten thousand years of peace, until he ascended

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:29.079
to the stars. Yi Ti was then ruled by the
Pearl Emperor, then the Jade, Tourmaline,

00:15:29.079 --> 00:15:36.050
Onyx, Topaz, and Opal Emperors, each reign
more troubled than the last. Until the Amethyst

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:42.670
Empress was killed and usurped by her brother,
the Bloodstone Emperor. He began a reign of

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:49.050
terror, practicing necromancy, slavery, cannibalism
and torture. He “took a tiger-woman for

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:53.829
his bride”, and worshipped “a black stone
that had fallen from the sky” – which

00:15:53.829 --> 00:15:57.620
might connect to the black stone on Yeen and
Toad Isle.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:03.500
It’s said that the Bloodstone Emperor caused
the Long Night, when the world went dark and

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:09.560
demons attacked. Yi Tish believe that the
Long Night was ended by the hero Azor Ahai

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:14.379
. So this seems to be the same story as the
Long Night in Westeros, when white walkers

00:16:14.379 --> 00:16:19.720
first attacked and were defeated by the last
hero. Yi Ti even has a structure like the

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:25.810
Wall – the huge Five Forts protect Yi Ti
from the “demons” of a “freezing desert”

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:33.310
. So did white walkers attack Yi Ti? Also,
the story of the Bloodstone Emperor is really

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:39.330
similar to the Westerosi story of the Night’s
King. They both marry a monstrous woman, make

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:45.389
themselves rulers, and worship dark forces
. These seem to be different cultures’ myths

00:16:45.389 --> 00:16:52.670
of the same events. So what really happened?
What caused the Long Night? And what ended

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:58.589
it? These questions are central to the last
season of Thrones – and the war to prevent

00:16:58.589 --> 00:17:06.490
a second Long Night. Another mystery is that
the Five Forts are made of “fused black

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:12.610
stone”. Different to the Lovecraftian oily
black stone, fused stone was made by Valyrians

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:18.669
with dragonflame . But the Five Forts predate
Valyria . So maybe the Great Empire of Yi

00:17:18.669 --> 00:17:25.169
Ti had dragons of their own. And another place
with ancient fused stone is the Hightower,

00:17:25.169 --> 00:17:30.990
in Westeros. Did ancient YiTish dragonriders
build the pyramids, I mean the Hightower?

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:35.960
We’ll go down that rabbithole in another
video. But check out LuciferMeansLightbringer

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:42.211
on YouTube who goes real deep on this stuff.
South of Yi Ti is the island of Leng. Its

00:17:42.211 --> 00:17:47.890
lush jungles are full of tigers and apes , and
it’s rich in “spices and gemstones”

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:52.240
. The people of Leng are some of the tallest
in the world, many reaching seven feet tall

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:57.539
– and they have better eyesight than other
humans . For most of its history, Leng was

00:17:57.539 --> 00:18:02.789
“an isle of mystery”, closed off to the
outside world. The Empress of Leng “was

00:18:02.789 --> 00:18:08.310
known to have congress with the Old Ones”
– gods who lived in ruined cities deep beneath

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:13.810
Leng’s jungles . Sometimes, the Old Ones
told the Empress to execute all the strangers

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:20.320
on the island . That stopped when Yi Ti invaded
Leng, and became the dominant people. The

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:24.630
ruined cities of the Old Ones were sealed
off. But “Legends persist that the Old Ones

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:32.050
still live” in the darkness below. So these
Old Ones are another clear reference to Lovecraft.

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:36.820
In fact, Leng is the name of a mysterious
interdimensional plateau in the Lovecraft

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:42.870
mythos . Further to the east, there’s also
the city of Carcosa, ruled by a yellow emperor,

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:47.860
and K’Dath, “where unspeakable rites are
performed” for “mad gods” . Author George

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:51.930
Martin has said that he added these Lovecraft
references basically just to fill out the

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:57.070
map – along with places like the City of
the Winged Men, Cities of the Bloodless Men,

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:03.900
and Bonetown. So these places are fun worldbuilding,
but probably not important to the story. There

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:08.850
is one city, though, that seems central to
the world of ice and fire.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:14.370
Asshai is “Easternmost and southernmost”
– “the end of the known world” . It’s

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:20.540
a huge city – bigger than King’s Landing,
Oldtown, Volantis and Qarth combined . And

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:27.040
Asshai is built entirely of Lovecraftian “greasy”
“black stone”, making Asshai dark and

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:33.700
gloomy even in summer . Though the city is
huge, the population is small. There are no

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:39.549
crowds or noisy markets – people walk “masked”
and “veiled” and alone . There are no

00:19:39.549 --> 00:19:45.820
children in Asshai , and no animals. Apparently,
they can’t survive the foul pollution of

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:51.620
the river Ash . The wider area’s called
the Shadow Lands, where glowing ghost grass

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:58.580
grows , and “dragons [stir]”. Asshai is
a centre of dark magic, where red priests,

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:04.750
bloodmages, necromancers, and night-walkers
practice their terrible spells in the night”

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:08.850
. Apparently, magic is stronger in Asshai
, and seekers come from all over the world

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:15.630
to learn secrets and magic. Melisandre, Quaithe,
Marwyn and Mirri Maz Duur all study magic

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:21.490
in Asshai. Euron Greyjoy claims to have come
and “and seen wonders and terrors beyond

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:26.750
imagining” . The masked “shadowbinders”,
like Melisandre and Quaithe, are said to be

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:32.380
the “Most sinister of all the sorcerers
of Asshai”. “They alone dare to go”

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:38.700
up the Ash deep into the Shadow Lands , where
there’s “demons and dragons and worse”.

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:45.120
In “the heart of darkness” lies “Stygai”,
“the City of the Night” , where even “shadowbinders

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:52.130
fear to tread” . So this place seems like
a cosmic centre of dark magic in the world.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:56.521
The “heart of darkness” is like an opposite
pole to “the heart of winter” in the north

00:20:56.521 --> 00:21:04.120
of Westeros . But who built Asshai ? And why
build a giant city out of “oily black stone”?

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:08.620
One theory is that the Bloodstone Emperor
built it – cause he worshipped black stone,

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:14.600
after all. Or maybe, Asshai used to be normal
stone, but some magical cataclysm like the

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:20.760
Long Night transformed it – the polluted
Shadowlands are like the fallout of some disaster,

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:26.750
like the Doom of Valyria. Or maybe Asshai
was built by the Lovecraftian Deep Ones – along

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:33.010
with the cities beneath Leng, and Yeen and
the toad stone. All these evil places seem

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:37.900
interconnected – the darkness of Asshai
runs deep.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:44.300
So the world of Game of Thrones is far bigger
than Westeros. It’s full of exotic creatures,

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:51.299
ancient peoples, uncomfortable race undertones,
Lovecraftian horrors, and cosmic mysteries.

00:21:51.299 --> 00:21:58.220
And these same forces of ice and fire are
playing out in the final season of Thrones.

00:21:58.220 --> 00:22:02.790
Much of the artwork in this video is from
Unseen Westeros, an exhibition of work by

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:08.550
forty Game of Thrones artists. You can see
the exhibition for free in Berlin in January.

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:14.870
Or you can get a beautiful artbook on their
Kickstarter. It’s got 80 pieces from Westeros

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:20.370
and beyond, many never-before-seen. This is
all non-profit, this isn’t sponsored, just

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:25.420
a celebration of the world of Thrones and
of the artists who bring it to life. The Kickstarter

00:22:25.420 --> 00:22:30.650
is the only way to get the book, and it closes
literally like today, so get it while you

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:34.000
can.
The map in this video is by Klaradox, and

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:39.120
other artwork’s by drafturgy, Mandy Finke,
Sanrixian, Kevin Catalan, Oriana Wiesner,

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:44.510
Matt Olson, and more. Links are below. Most
of the info from this video is from the World

00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:49.940
of Ice and Fire, you can pick that up on Amazon
to support Alt Shift X at no extra cost to

00:22:49.940 --> 00:22:54.140
you. Thank you for watching. Please like and
